What:		/sys/devices/platform/180f0000.wifi/factory_mac_address
Date:		October 2026
Contact:		A1260 kernel maintainers
Description:
		Factory Wi-Fi MAC supplied by privileged board initialization before
		the first radio start. Accepts six colon-separated hexadecimal octets,
		optionally followed by a newline. Multicast, all-zero and broadcast
		addresses are rejected. Reads return the provisioned address or unset.

		The address is write-once for this boot. Repeating the same value is
		allowed; a different value returns EBUSY. If the radio has already
		consulted an unset value, subsequent provisioning also returns EBUSY.
		No active netdev address or calibration record is modified by a write.

		A valid NVRAM address retains precedence. Otherwise the driver uses
		this factory value, then a valid embedded NIC address, then a locally
		administered random fallback cached for the rest of the boot.
